.TH ADMIN 5 "October 2026" "apkg 0.3.4" "Amix File Formats"
.SH NAME
admin \- installation defaults for pkgadd and pkgrm; apkg's /var/apkg/admin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /var/apkg/admin
.SH DESCRIPTION
An admin file answers in advance the questions
.BR pkgadd (1M)
and
.BR pkgrm (1M)
would otherwise ask, so they can run without a terminal.  It is passed
with
.B \-a
.IR file .
Each line is
.IB keyword = value\fR.
.PP
.BR apkg (1)
runs every pkgadd and pkgrm with
.B /var/apkg/admin
(the
.B admin
key of
.BR apkg.conf (5)),
because the engine's input is not a terminal.  The file is a
.BR conffile (5)
of the APKG package: an upgrade keeps your edited file and puts the new
default beside it as
.BR /var/apkg/admin.new .
.B apkg
re-creates the file with the default contents if it is missing, and never
rewrites an existing one.
.SH KEYWORDS
Each keyword takes
.B nocheck
(do not check),
.B quit
(stop the installation) or
.B ask
(ask; with no terminal this is a failure), except where noted.
.TP 12
.B mail
users to mail when an installation finishes (empty: nobody)
.TP
.B instance
what to do when the package is already installed:
.B quit
(stop),
.B overwrite
(install over it), or
.B unique
(install a second instance)
.TP
.B partial
an earlier installation of the package was not completed
.TP
.B runlevel
the system is not at the run level the package asks for
.TP
.B idepend
a package this one depends on is not installed
.TP
.B rdepend
removing the package would break a package that depends on it
.TP
.B space
the file systems lack the space the package needs
.TP
.B setuid
the package installs setuid or setgid files
.TP
.B conflict
the package installs files another package owns
.TP
.B action
the package runs install scripts
.TP
.B basedir
the installation base directory
.RB ( default :
the package's own
.BR BASEDIR )
.SH APKG'S DEFAULT
.nf
mail=
instance=quit
partial=nocheck
runlevel=nocheck
idepend=nocheck
rdepend=nocheck
space=quit
setuid=nocheck
conflict=nocheck
action=nocheck
basedir=default
.fi
.PP
Dependencies are checked by
.B apkg
itself before the engine runs, so the engine's own checks are off.
For an upgrade,
.B apkg
derives
.B /var/apkg/admin.overwrite
from this file: every keyword you set is carried across and only
.B instance
becomes
.BR overwrite .
.SH FILES
.PD 0
.TP 28
.B /var/apkg/admin
apkg's admin file
.TP
.B /var/apkg/admin.new
the new default after an upgrade that kept your file
.TP
.B /var/apkg/admin.overwrite
derived for upgrades; rewritten on every use
.PD
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apkg (1),
.BR apkg.conf (5),
.BR conffile (5),
.BR pkgadd (1M),
.BR pkgrm (1M)
